## 🔍 Phase 1: Workflow Mapping

In the `01.AudioFileInfo` exercise, we mapped out the complete data flow and core objects from a file path to reading audio metadata:

### 1. Core Objects & Fill-in-the-Blanks

1. **`juce::File`**: Object representing the file on disk.
2. **`juce::AudioFormatManager`**: Manages different audio formats (WAV, AIFF, etc.).
3. **`juce::AudioFormatReader`**: Reads audio data and provides file information.
4. **`std::unique_ptr`**: Used for automatic memory management (RAII principle).
5. **`if (reader)` check**: Ensures the reader pointer is valid to prevent crashes if the file fails to open or format is unsupported.

### 2. Data Flow

$$\text{File path} \longrightarrow \text{juce::File} \longrightarrow \text{AudioFormatManager / Reader} \longrightarrow \text{Audio Information}$$

